[I] Statistical toolkit for criminology and sociolegal research

[T] A command-line tool and C library, written in C++17 with no dependencies,
[T] of statistical methods for criminology and sociolegal research.
[T] Use it to test a stop record for disparity, weigh DNA and score-based
[T] evidence, evaluate a policy, audit a risk score, and describe sentences,
[T] custody and crime places.

[U] https://crimlab.dev/

[A] Vansh Singh Ruhela
[M] Vansh Singh Ruhela <vsruhela@proton.me>

[C] extra/scientific

[L] APL
[V] 0.0.4
[P] X -----5---9 200.000

[D] 12ccf44b3fd8fa898c99c2cf49f72dc90ce812175ae81ca3bf2d4aae crimlab-0.0.4.tar.gz https://github.com/rootcoder007/crimlab/releases/download/v0.0.4/

hook_add premake 5 'cd cli'
# one 'install -d' names four directories; the install wrapper takes the
# last, when it exists, as the target of those that do not exist yet
hook_add inmake 4 'mkdir -p $root/$prefix/include/crimlab'
var_append makeopt ' ' 'WERROR= LIBDIR=$libdir'
var_append makeinstopt ' ' 'WERROR= LIBDIR=$root$libdir'
